design\releases\0_3_0\F_182_move_context_size_to_below_chatlog.md:29:- Align metadata-row items on one baseline. Keep status and duration on the left; render `context: N%` on the right with caption styling. Use flexible space so context stays right-aligned.
design\releases\0_3_0\F_182_move_context_size_to_below_chatlog.md:30:- Show `ConversationTimer` whenever a conversation exists, including when popup status is `idle`. Keep status text hidden for `idle`. `ConversationTimer` must schedule ticks only while status is `running`; for `idle`, waiting, completed, failed, or cancelled states it displays its current or completed value without advancing.
design\releases\0_3_0\F_182_move_context_size_to_below_chatlog.md:33:- Use the live conversation while a run exists; otherwise use the selected persisted conversation. Switching conversations must update duration and context metadata together.
design\releases\0_3_0\F_182_move_context_size_to_below_chatlog.md:34:- No desktop, persistence, or conversation-schema change is required because F_122 already stores and restores `contextWindowUsage`.
design\releases\0_3_0\F_182_move_context_size_to_below_chatlog.md:39:- Conversation with `usedTokens = 42,000` and `capacityTokens = 258,400` shows `context: 16%` at right of metadata row below chatlog, level with duration timer.
